      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Most environmental policy experts view well-designed congestion pricing as a necessary and powerful tool to achieve significant, targeted reductions in urban emissions. Because it directly targets the source of the problem (frequent, stop-and-go driving in dense areas), it is often seen as more effective than broad emission standards alone. Therefore, for serious climate-focused advocates, it is a crucial, not just optional, part of the necessary policy mix for sustainable urban living.",
      "source": "target",
